# Linda: bank teller, or feminist bank teller?
subtitle: "Meet Linda, then pick the likelier story about her. See why most people choose wrong, and how two circles expose the conjunction fallacy."

## Linda: bank teller, or feminist bank teller?
sources:
    - id: tk
      title: 'Extensional versus intuitive reasoning: the conjunction fallacy in probability judgment'
      authors: A. Tversky, D. Kahneman
      year: 1983
      doi: 10.1037/0033-295X.90.4.293
      finding: about 85 % of respondents ranked 'bank teller and active in the feminist movement' as more probable than 'bank teller'
    - id: gould
      title: Bully for Brontosaurus
      authors: S. J. Gould
      year: 1991
      finding: Gould wrote that a homunculus in his head kept shouting that Linda can't just be a bank teller

    person linda "" #2f6b8f x 230 y 450 width 230 height 300 hidden true
    text linda_l "Linda" #2f6b8f x 230 y 255 font_size 48 hidden true
    text t1 "31, outspoken" x 650 y 570 font_size 48 hidden true
    text t2 "philosophy major" x 650 y 490 font_size 48 hidden true
    text t3 "fights discrimination" x 650 y 410 font_size 48 hidden true
    text t4 "anti-nuclear marches" x 650 y 330 font_size 48 hidden true
    ellipse tellers #2f6b8f x 500 y 445 rx 420 ry 195 hidden true
    text tellers_l "Bank tellers" #2f6b8f x 250 y 445 font_size 48 hidden true
    ellipse fem #b5482e x 630 y 400 rx 200 ry 115 hidden true
    text fem_l "+ feminist" #b5482e x 630 y 435 font_size 44 hidden true
    text conj "conjunction fallacy" #b5482e cites ["tk"] x 500 y 205 font_size 44 hidden true
    box bubble "She can't just be a bank teller!" cites ["gould"] x 370 y 590 width 600 height 80 font_size 42 style.fill #fbf3df hidden true

    card title "Which is more probable?"

A: Here's a famous puzzle about a woman called Linda. Which story about her is more probable?
    draw linda linda_l

A: Linda is thirty-one, single, outspoken and very bright.
    draw t1

A: She studied philosophy. As a student she cared deeply about discrimination, and marched against nuclear weapons.
    draw t2 t3 t4

    quiz "Which is more probable?"
        right: Bank teller. Every feminist bank teller is a bank teller too, so the pair can never be more likely.
        wrong: Count what each answer needs to be true.
        + Linda is a bank teller
        * Linda is a bank teller and a feminist

B: But she sounds exactly like a feminist!
    highlight t3 t4

    erase linda linda_l t1 t2 t3 t4

A: She does. But draw it. Here are all the bank tellers in the world.
    draw tellers tellers_l

A: The feminist bank tellers are a group inside that one. However likely the story, the inner group can't be bigger.
    draw fem fem_l

A: Yet in Tversky and Kahneman's 1983 study, about eighty-five percent of people picked the second answer.
    text pct "85 % chose it" #b5482e cites ["tk"] x 630 y 365 font_size 38

B: So more detail made the story feel more likely?
    highlight fem fem_l

A: Exactly. They called it the conjunction fallacy: each added detail makes a story less likely, but more believable.
    draw conj

B: Even the biologist Stephen Jay Gould admitted a little voice in his head kept shouting: but she can't just be a bank teller!
    draw bubble
---
